{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488822-child-kithain-and-how-to-portray-them","id":1488822,"title":"Child Kithain and how to portray them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-02T08:06:39-07:00","id":1488822,"title":"Child Kithain and how to portray them","content":"I've been pretty much absent from CtD since early 2e, despite actually loving it, because my group never cared much for the game. Anyway, I've recently returned to C20 which rekindled my love for the game. <br /> <br /> Child characters have been part of CtD since 1e. Back then in the early days, when playing CtD outside my group from time to time, I encountered various ways how players portrayed child (and often Childling) characters\u2014sometimes as genuinely childlike as possible, often as bratty little adults, and sometimes even as overly mature &quot;old soul&quot; children.<br /> <br /> I assume that basically all of the above is probably covered by the lore. Of course, having an immortal faerie soul and possibly faint memories of centuries of rebirths will probably mature a child's personality.<br /> <br /> Still, I wonder... how do you prefer to portray child characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:42:48-07:00","id":1488830,"title":"","content":"In theory, the same way you describe. In practice, I have trouble getting into the mindset of children; I prefer to restrict myself to Grumps, because they're the only Seeming that I can play properly. It's a failing on my part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T11:51:46-07:00","id":1488860,"title":"","content":"I remember what it was like to be a kid, and also think about kids I know both now and in the past","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T12:17:13-07:00","id":1488866,"title":"","content":"I think you could justify a lot. It just depends. A pooka would probably be more childish, but a bit wise beyond their years. Other Kiths might act more like a precocious child, or something else appropriate to their nature.<br /> <br /> And the amount of Banality would probably be approrpriate to factor it. The more Banal, the more likely the childer will act like a human child than an old fae in its body as the &quot;reality&quot; of being a human child asserts itself. But acting appropriately in their Mortal Seeming would prevent Banality from intruding and risk increasing their Banality. So a fae might switch personas between the two.<br /> <br /> Having a variety of acceptable portrayals, but which makes sense given the specifics of the character, would help distinguish the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T00:42:11-07:00","id":1488947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1488822-child-kithain-and-how-to-portray-them?p=1488830#post1488830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, the same way you describe. In practice, I have trouble getting into the mindset of children; I prefer to restrict myself to Grumps, because they're the only Seeming that I can play properly. It's a failing on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, it would be interesting to know how many groups either ignore or disallow Childling characters.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not particularly good with children and I also have problems getting into a childlike mindset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}